body:
Agent-guide reference file: each kalide author guide is delivered to a project as a kalide-owned full guide file plus a short pointer file that names it. The full guide is `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` at the project root (the deck guide, agent-authoring, for a deck) or the library root (the library guide, library-agent-guide, for a template library). The pointer is the project's own `AGENTS.md`.

The reference line is the exact string `Kalide Reference: ./AGENTS_KALIDE.md`. The embedded pointer scaffold content is a fixed short header line followed by that reference line, and the header line is `# kalide authoring guide`; a created `AGENTS.md` carries exactly that embedded pointer content.

The pointer rule is idempotent and author-preserving:
- `AGENTS.md` absent: it is created carrying the embedded pointer content above;
- `AGENTS.md` present and already containing the exact string `Kalide Reference: ./AGENTS_KALIDE.md`: it is left byte-for-byte untouched;
- `AGENTS.md` present without that string and byte-identical to a known released full guide of either author guide: `kalide upgrade` replaces it with the short pointer file and writes the current `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` (upgrade-refresh-owned-scaffold, global.constraint.upgrade-known-version-catalog);
- `AGENTS.md` present without that string and not a known released full guide (author content): the reference line is appended and the author's existing content is byte-preserved.

The exact set of permitted modifications of `AGENTS.md` is: creation when it is absent; appending the reference line to an author file without the string; and the `kalide upgrade` replacement of a known released full guide. A scaffolding command performs only creation and append; the replacement belongs to upgrade alone. No other write to `AGENTS.md` occurs, and the embedded pointer content's header line and reference line are fixed.

The full guide is written only when `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` is absent (an existing `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` is kalide-owned and brought forward by `kalide upgrade`, upgrade-refresh-owned-scaffold). Both files are text-only, offline, inert to load/validate/render/serve/list, and not template assets (global.constraint.no-embedded-template-assets, solution.constraint.agent-guide-unbranded-inert).

AC:
- immediately after any scaffolding command, `<root>/AGENTS_KALIDE.md` holds the full guide and `<root>/AGENTS.md` contains the string `Kalide Reference: ./AGENTS_KALIDE.md`;
- an `AGENTS.md` created by a scaffolding command carries the fixed header line `# kalide authoring guide` followed by the reference line;
- a project whose `AGENTS.md` already contains the string is left byte-for-byte unchanged by a further scaffolding or upgrade run;
- a project whose `AGENTS.md` is author content without the string gains the appended reference line, with all its other bytes unchanged;
- a project whose `AGENTS.md` is byte-identical to a known released full guide has it replaced by the short pointer file by `kalide upgrade`, and the current `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` is written;
- neither file is read by `kalide start` or `kalide templates`: a project holding both loads, validates, renders, serves and lists unchanged.
